      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "L174-A12-master-net-attribution",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L174"
      },
      "rationale": "The master net's two sides, their counters and the code side's hasSidecar flags are one cached_read under ('master-net', repo_id, master, selection.digest, onboarding root), and selection.digest is the sha256 over the four endpoint commits. A hit returns a deep copy of the stored net with no observation and no native diff, so the served net is byte-identical to the native read for those endpoints; every route index and fallback mirror path the sidecar decision consults is observed before it is read, so a moved onboarding input re-keys instead of leaving a stale flag. The per-leaf rows and the endpoint selection stay outside the retained value.",
      "role": "support"
    }
  ],
